K-FOG: Role-Owned Choice and Dependent Interaction

The current manuscript is main.tex and its root-level inputs. Build it with:

    make paper

The PDF is written to build/main.pdf. The build uses latexmk, pdfLaTeX, and
BibTeX. Run the finite semantic checks and verify the original archive with:

    make check

This is a research draft, with the novelty question stated explicitly in
the introduction. The public dependent core is background from dependent
interaction and session typing. Full strategies are retained separately
from executable plans. A finite rational-outcome algebra records the winners
of pure subgame-perfect profiles. The disclosure section has a protocol
grammar, phase typing, audience-derived views, and a two-execution hiding
theorem for prefixes excluding dependency-mediated releases.

General open-network cut, a complete logical proof calculus, and control
operators are development targets. The Python checks exercise only the
finite models, not the dependent data calculus or a proof assistant.

The previous manuscript, including its bibliography and interpreter sketch,
is preserved in archive/manuscript-2026-10-28. MANIFEST.sha256 records each
original file's content hash. Independent notes/ and research/ material is
retained separately and is not an input to the current paper.

The first public-core rewrite, before responding to the external review,
is preserved in archive/public-core-draft-2026-10-28 with its own manifest.
Both archives are verified by make check.

The next research iteration is in research/minimal/report.tex. It studies
only finite public owned binary choice: optimal syntactic occurrence cost
of neutral union, uniform-copy SPE preservation, and unary normal forms.
Run make check-minimal for Lean and finite checks, and make paper-minimal
for build/minimal/report.pdf. The directory README distinguishes generic
proofs from mathematical arguments and finite experiments. These results
are candidates for an algebraic contribution; priority remains open.
